# Merge quality gate (mandatory)

**Never merge a PR to `main` if any required check is red or pending.**
**Never `git push origin main` to bypass that gate.**

## When a PR is green — merge it

Once the gate below is fully green, **merge the PR without waiting to be asked**. Prefer the repo default merge method via `gh pr merge`. Then pull `main` locally and delete the finished feature branch.

Do this for every PR you open or are watching in the session (including ones that turn green after a fix push).

## Before every merge

```bash
gh pr checks <number>
npm run sonar:gate -- --status --pr <number>
```

Do not merge until **all** of the following are `pass` (or `skipping` when expected):

| Check | When required |
|---|---|
| **SonarCloud Code Analysis** | Always (GitHub required check on `main`) |
| **SonarCloud quality gate** | Always when that workflow runs (waits on the App check) |
| **Lint and build** | Web paths changed (see `web-quality.yml`) — includes `npm test`, unit sweep, production build, Playwright portal phases 1–2 |
| **Game QA** | Version tags `v*` and manual dispatch (see `game-qa.yml`); same web job, no path filter |
| **Build debug APK** | Android paths changed (see `android-native.yml`) |
| **Polyglot checks** | Polyglot paths changed (see `polyglot-quality.yml`) |

A missing path-filtered job is **not** a failure. Do not wait for `Build debug APK` on a pytest-only PR. If SonarCloud is `fail` or pending, **stop**.

Do not push to `main`. Do not bypass branch protection.

Owner: keep `SonarCloud Code Analysis` required. Do **not** require path-filtered jobs (`Lint and build`, `Build debug APK`, `Polyglot checks`) on every PR — they skip when their paths do not match.

PR #121 was merged with Sonar red (`Math.random()` in `lib/boss-api-handlers.js`), breaking the main quality gate. That must not happen again.
